WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:02.819
- And you may not know
it, but some of the people

00:00:02.819 --> 00:00:04.377
that are giving you the most trouble

00:00:04.377 --> 00:00:07.275
may be helping you more than anybody.

00:00:07.275 --> 00:00:10.700
You have no idea how frighteningly average

00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:13.562
and normal I am, if you
have a habit of just talking

00:00:13.562 --> 00:00:15.959
about your problems all the time,

00:00:15.959 --> 00:00:18.363
it's time to make a new habit.

00:00:18.363 --> 00:00:20.670
Bunch of people old
before their times because

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:23.592
they look like, they're 40
and look like they're 90

00:00:23.592 --> 00:00:26.456
because they've worried
themselves to death.

00:00:26.456 --> 00:00:28.886
- She's a charismatic
Christian speaker, author,

00:00:28.886 --> 00:00:31.536
and pastor, she speaks
humorously with her audience,

00:00:31.536 --> 00:00:34.017
sharing her personal
stories and often taking

00:00:34.017 --> 00:00:37.001
small jabs at stereotypical
church behavior.

00:00:37.001 --> 00:00:40.460
Time magazine also named her
one of the 25 most influential

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.231
evangelicals in America,
she's Joyce Meyer,

00:00:43.231 --> 00:00:46.647
and here's my take on her
top 10 rules for success.

00:00:46.647 --> 00:00:47.800
Rule number four is my personal favorite,

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:49.842
and I'd love to know which
ones you guys like the best.

00:00:49.842 --> 00:00:51.614
Also, as Joyce is talking,
if she says something

00:00:51.614 --> 00:00:54.296
that really resonates
with you, please leave it

00:00:54.296 --> 00:00:56.007
in the comments below
and put quotes around it

00:00:56.007 --> 00:00:58.042
so other people can be inspired as well

00:00:58.042 --> 00:01:00.626
and also when you write it
down, it helps lock it in

00:01:00.626 --> 00:01:03.038
for yourself, enjoy.

00:01:03.038 --> 00:01:05.621
(upbeat music)

00:01:15.839 --> 00:01:18.008
- I tell a story about
a poor pitiful donkey

00:01:18.008 --> 00:01:21.384
that got thrown down into a
well, he fell into a well,

00:01:21.384 --> 00:01:25.551
and the farmer heard this
donkey crying in the well

00:01:26.489 --> 00:01:30.239
and he was trying to
debate on whether or not

00:01:32.703 --> 00:01:36.109
to try to get him out or
not, the well was deep

00:01:36.109 --> 00:01:37.590
and it was going to be a lot of hard work

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:41.511
and the donkey was old anyway
and so maybe we'll just

00:01:41.511 --> 00:01:44.222
bury him and let it go, so he went and got

00:01:44.222 --> 00:01:47.540
a bunch of friends and
said, let's just bury him,

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.134
help me shovel some dirt
in there, so he'll shut up

00:01:50.134 --> 00:01:52.838
that crying, he's an old
donkey and not worth too much

00:01:52.838 --> 00:01:54.709
anyway, you know, there
may be a lot of people

00:01:54.709 --> 00:01:56.489
that just think you're just an old donkey

00:01:56.489 --> 00:01:59.441
and not worth too much anyway,

00:01:59.441 --> 00:02:00.988
maybe feel like you're in a pit right now

00:02:00.988 --> 00:02:03.830
and somebody's shoveling dirt on you.

00:02:03.830 --> 00:02:06.404
But what are you going to do about it?

00:02:06.404 --> 00:02:08.264
Well, the donkey's down
there and he's crying out

00:02:08.264 --> 00:02:11.181
pitifully. (brays)

00:02:17.463 --> 00:02:19.779
And here comes a shovelful
of dirt and another shovelful

00:02:19.779 --> 00:02:22.637
and a shovelful of dirt, and
it would hit him on the back,

00:02:22.637 --> 00:02:23.887
and he'd go ...

00:02:24.972 --> 00:02:27.996
(audience laughs)

00:02:27.996 --> 00:02:31.259
Get on top of it, here
comes some more dirt

00:02:31.259 --> 00:02:33.302
and some more dirt and some more dirt.

00:02:33.302 --> 00:02:37.324
He'd shake it off his back,
he'd wiggle just a little.

00:02:37.324 --> 00:02:39.314
He couldn't get out of the
pit, but he could wiggle

00:02:39.314 --> 00:02:41.534
and he'd get up on top of that dirt

00:02:41.534 --> 00:02:43.490
and he was getting closer
and closer to the top

00:02:43.490 --> 00:02:47.151
and pretty soon he just
walked right out of that pit.

00:02:47.151 --> 00:02:48.247
(audience cheers)

00:02:48.247 --> 00:02:49.780
All those people shoveling
dirt on him helped him

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:51.363
get out of the pit.

00:02:55.102 --> 00:02:57.894
Are you out there tonight?

00:02:57.894 --> 00:02:59.650
All those people shoveling dirt on him

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:01.584
actually helped him,
and you may not know it

00:03:01.584 --> 00:03:03.565
but some of the people that are giving you

00:03:03.565 --> 00:03:06.047
the most trouble may be helping you more

00:03:06.047 --> 00:03:10.214
than anybody, are you living
an unsustainable life?

00:03:11.086 --> 00:03:14.611
Do you find yourself saying,
I can't do this much longer?

00:03:14.611 --> 00:03:18.119
I just can't keep this up forever.

00:03:18.119 --> 00:03:22.131
This is just too much for me,
or are other people telling

00:03:22.131 --> 00:03:26.117
you you can't keep going
on like this forever?

00:03:26.117 --> 00:03:28.987
How many of you got some people
in your life that love you

00:03:28.987 --> 00:03:31.195
telling you you can't keep
this up, you can't keep

00:03:31.195 --> 00:03:33.523
doing this, you're going
to have to slow down,

00:03:33.523 --> 00:03:35.052
you're going to have
to lay something down,

00:03:35.052 --> 00:03:36.657
you're going to have to give something up?

00:03:36.657 --> 00:03:39.533
Well Moses had the same
thing, he was overloaded

00:03:39.533 --> 00:03:42.395
but to be honest I don't
know that he really knew it

00:03:42.395 --> 00:03:44.076
and you know, I'm such a
hard worker that sometimes

00:03:44.076 --> 00:03:48.266
I can not even realize
that I'm doing too much,

00:03:48.266 --> 00:03:50.621
sometimes I don't even know
when I'm being excessive

00:03:50.621 --> 00:03:54.571
and somebody has to come
along and say, wait a minute,

00:03:54.571 --> 00:03:56.327
you're not going to do
that, you just got back

00:03:56.327 --> 00:03:59.381
from a conference, you're going to rest,

00:03:59.381 --> 00:04:01.676
so sometimes it pays to
listen to other people.

00:04:01.676 --> 00:04:02.759
Exodus 18:14.

00:04:06.514 --> 00:04:08.513
"When Moses' father in
law saw what he was doing

00:04:08.513 --> 00:04:12.680
"for the people, he said,
what is this that you do

00:04:13.687 --> 00:04:16.067
"for the people, why do you sit alone

00:04:16.067 --> 00:04:20.234
"and the people stand around
you from morning till evening?

00:04:21.124 --> 00:04:25.758
Now listen, Mom, why do
you wait on your children

00:04:25.758 --> 00:04:29.295
hand and foot while they
sit around and watch you

00:04:29.295 --> 00:04:31.592
and do nothing but play on
their iPads from morning

00:04:31.592 --> 00:04:33.077
till evening?

00:04:33.077 --> 00:04:35.910
(audience cheers)

00:04:41.097 --> 00:04:43.930
Well ... (laughs)

00:04:48.365 --> 00:04:49.521
Let me tell you something,
that kid of yours

00:04:49.521 --> 00:04:50.712
can put cereal in a bowl.

00:04:50.712 --> 00:04:53.600
(audience cheers)

00:04:53.600 --> 00:04:54.664
They might make a little mess,

00:04:54.664 --> 00:04:57.149
but it won't be the end of the world.

00:04:57.149 --> 00:04:58.691
If you're enjoying yourself
sitting in your recliner

00:04:58.691 --> 00:05:02.774
and you're relaxing, let
'em get their own snack.

00:05:05.048 --> 00:05:08.072
Oh, boy, come on, I don't
want to work this hard

00:05:08.072 --> 00:05:12.579
on Friday night, why do you
sit alone while everybody

00:05:12.579 --> 00:05:16.793
stands around you, now you
don't all have that problem

00:05:16.793 --> 00:05:19.876
but I have a daughter that does that.

00:05:21.239 --> 00:05:23.712
You can just get into
habits and the way you start

00:05:23.712 --> 00:05:27.655
with people is what they're
going to expect later on,

00:05:27.655 --> 00:05:30.142
so then if you've already
got a bunch of bad habits

00:05:30.142 --> 00:05:32.459
in your house, then it's
going to really kind of shock

00:05:32.459 --> 00:05:35.252
everybody when you kind
of bring down the gauntlet

00:05:35.252 --> 00:05:37.817
and say I'm not going to
live like this anymore,

00:05:37.817 --> 00:05:39.056
and they're going to
think you're being mean

00:05:39.056 --> 00:05:40.932
and think you're being
bad and so there'll be

00:05:40.932 --> 00:05:42.693
a little time of adjustment

00:05:42.693 --> 00:05:44.382
and it doesn't mean you don't do anything

00:05:44.382 --> 00:05:49.314
for anybody but don't let
people take advantage of you,

00:05:49.314 --> 00:05:52.145
have some boundaries and some borders.

00:05:52.145 --> 00:05:53.261
Some of you need a laugh right now,

00:05:53.261 --> 00:05:55.245
so I'm going to stop right in
the middle of this preaching

00:05:55.245 --> 00:05:57.207
and tell you a joke.

00:05:57.207 --> 00:06:00.040
(audience laughs)

00:06:01.571 --> 00:06:05.738
Well, honey, I've never been
in a church like this, well,

00:06:06.835 --> 00:06:09.539
two old people were laying
in bed side by side.

00:06:09.539 --> 00:06:13.372
I'm talking really old,
like, wrinkled up old.

00:06:16.728 --> 00:06:20.356
And she said, honey, why don't you ever

00:06:20.356 --> 00:06:23.779
hold my hand like you used to at night?

00:06:23.779 --> 00:06:25.967
So his little old wrinkled
hand came across the bed

00:06:25.967 --> 00:06:29.384
and he took her little old wrinkled hand,

00:06:30.592 --> 00:06:32.612
she said, honey, why
don't you ever hold me

00:06:32.612 --> 00:06:36.210
in your arms like you used to at night?

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:37.922
So he sighed and it
took him a little while

00:06:37.922 --> 00:06:41.172
but he got over to her side of the bed,

00:06:42.007 --> 00:06:46.149
got her in his arms and
she rested a little bit

00:06:46.149 --> 00:06:48.738
and then she said,
honey, why don't you ever

00:06:48.738 --> 00:06:52.905
nibble on my ear like you
used to at night? (laughs)

00:06:56.378 --> 00:06:58.261
And all of a sudden he
jumped up and started

00:06:58.261 --> 00:06:59.983
across the floor, and she said,
well, where are you going,

00:06:59.983 --> 00:07:02.041
and he said, well, I got to get my teeth.

00:07:02.041 --> 00:07:04.874
(audience laughs)

00:07:16.526 --> 00:07:18.650
Now see, you're thinking,
well, what does that have to do

00:07:18.650 --> 00:07:23.088
with anything, nothing, it has
nothing to do with anything

00:07:23.088 --> 00:07:26.357
and that's exactly what you
need to get through your head

00:07:26.357 --> 00:07:29.346
that everything doesn't
have to have some big

00:07:29.346 --> 00:07:31.511
super duper purpose.

00:07:31.511 --> 00:07:34.824
(audience cheers)

00:07:34.824 --> 00:07:37.272
It's okay to just stop right
in the middle of some work

00:07:37.272 --> 00:07:39.402
and just have a little bit of fun,

00:07:39.402 --> 00:07:41.449
matter of fact, you
could laugh at yourself

00:07:41.449 --> 00:07:44.193
and lighten up your life a whole lot.

00:07:44.193 --> 00:07:45.217
Look at me and let me tell you something,

00:07:45.217 --> 00:07:49.384
you can believe what you
want to believe. (laughs)

00:07:52.297 --> 00:07:55.559
You're going to believe
something, it might as well

00:07:55.559 --> 00:07:58.559
be something that is going to help you.

00:08:00.146 --> 00:08:02.315
It's just as simple, actually,
it's easier to believe

00:08:02.315 --> 00:08:05.978
you can than to believe you can't.

00:08:05.978 --> 00:08:07.994
It's easier to believe
you are than to believe

00:08:07.994 --> 00:08:10.646
you aren't, now, you know,
based on what you guys

00:08:10.646 --> 00:08:14.313
tell me, you love me,
you like me, you know,

00:08:15.419 --> 00:08:18.491
you tell me, I think you're
this, I think you're that,

00:08:18.491 --> 00:08:20.534
blah blah blah, you've changed my life,

00:08:20.534 --> 00:08:24.701
you have no idea how frighteningly
average and normal I am.

00:08:26.196 --> 00:08:29.029
(audience laughs)

00:08:30.950 --> 00:08:32.343
I mean, it's like sometimes
I'm walking around

00:08:32.343 --> 00:08:34.718
and somebody'll run up
to me and say (screams)

00:08:34.718 --> 00:08:38.939
You're Joyce Meyer, and I'm,
like, oh, yeah, oh yeah,

00:08:38.939 --> 00:08:42.439
I'm Joyce Meyer. (laughs)

00:08:45.135 --> 00:08:48.802
(audience cheers and claps)

00:08:53.236 --> 00:08:57.979
But see, actually the
truth is I'm just like you

00:08:57.979 --> 00:09:01.976
and you're just like me,
we're all just a big mess.

00:09:01.976 --> 00:09:03.641
(audience laughs)

00:09:03.641 --> 00:09:06.476
With Jesus living on the
inside, saying you got

00:09:06.476 --> 00:09:10.294
what it takes, if there is any difference

00:09:10.294 --> 00:09:13.256
in me and you and there
doesn't have to be,

00:09:13.256 --> 00:09:15.960
but if there is any, it's
only because I've decided

00:09:15.960 --> 00:09:20.127
to believe it and you haven't
quite decided that yet.

00:09:22.837 --> 00:09:26.181
You can get over a broken
past if you decide to believe

00:09:26.181 --> 00:09:28.367
that there's nothing in
your past that can keep you

00:09:28.367 --> 00:09:30.317
from having a great future.

00:09:30.317 --> 00:09:34.258
First Peter 5:8 says be well balanced,

00:09:34.258 --> 00:09:37.612
are you living a balanced life?

00:09:37.612 --> 00:09:41.424
How many of you don't get enough sleep,

00:09:41.424 --> 00:09:44.896
no matter where I go, it's the same thing,

00:09:44.896 --> 00:09:47.884
80% of the people don't get enough sleep,

00:09:47.884 --> 00:09:51.806
well, what's going to
fix it, start sleeping.

00:09:51.806 --> 00:09:54.639
(audience laughs)

00:09:58.225 --> 00:10:02.421
(laughs) That's simple, get more sleep.

00:10:02.421 --> 00:10:05.250
Well, I can't sleep, I
have trouble sleeping,

00:10:05.250 --> 00:10:06.823
well, don't spend all day worrying,

00:10:06.823 --> 00:10:09.608
then maybe you'll be able
to go to sleep at night.

00:10:09.608 --> 00:10:13.025
How many of you don't drink enough water?

00:10:14.502 --> 00:10:17.088
Well, we can fix that too, drink water.

00:10:17.088 --> 00:10:19.647
(audience laughs)

00:10:19.647 --> 00:10:23.260
This is not rocket science, I
mean, I'm trying to tell you

00:10:23.260 --> 00:10:26.583
tonight that you can fix your life faster

00:10:26.583 --> 00:10:29.410
than you think you can fix your life.

00:10:29.410 --> 00:10:31.393
Fear is something that's not ever
going to completely disappear

00:10:31.393 --> 00:10:34.457
from our lives, the
feeling of fear is not ever

00:10:34.457 --> 00:10:37.757
going to completely disappear,
and just because you feel fear

00:10:37.757 --> 00:10:42.181
that doesn't mean that
you have to be afraid,

00:10:42.181 --> 00:10:44.177
and I don't know about you,
but that was a great revelation

00:10:44.177 --> 00:10:47.175
to me many years ago
because I kept wanting

00:10:47.175 --> 00:10:51.529
to not feel afraid and God
wanted me to feel the fear

00:10:51.529 --> 00:10:56.108
and be courageous anyway,
courage means to go ahead

00:10:56.108 --> 00:10:58.837
and take the action that
you believe you should take

00:10:58.837 --> 00:11:00.781
or that you know that
God wants you to take

00:11:00.781 --> 00:11:02.448
while you feel fear.

00:11:04.206 --> 00:11:08.591
We let our feelings
dictate to us way too much,

00:11:08.591 --> 00:11:10.618
and so the only acceptable
attitude that a Christian can

00:11:10.618 --> 00:11:13.201
have is simply I will not fear.

00:11:15.179 --> 00:11:18.429
So let's all say that, I will not fear.

00:11:20.285 --> 00:11:21.569
Now, once again, that doesn't mean

00:11:21.569 --> 00:11:23.588
that you'll never feel
fear, matter of fact,

00:11:23.588 --> 00:11:25.551
I can pretty much
promise you that you will

00:11:25.551 --> 00:11:29.620
but it does mean that
you can feel the fear,

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:33.412
do whatever you believe
that you're supposed to do

00:11:33.412 --> 00:11:38.098
while you feel afraid, you
can learn to do it afraid

00:11:38.098 --> 00:11:40.608
if that's the only way that you can do it.

00:11:40.608 --> 00:11:42.366
Don't let the feelings
of fear keep you trapped

00:11:42.366 --> 00:11:44.933
any longer, now first
of all, let me say this,

00:11:44.933 --> 00:11:47.933
a positive attitude attracts people,

00:11:49.778 --> 00:11:53.777
a negative attitude
usually doesn't win you

00:11:53.777 --> 00:11:57.338
very many friends, now,
I don't want to hurt

00:11:57.338 --> 00:11:59.441
anybody's feelings, but I
just want to throw this out

00:11:59.441 --> 00:12:03.358
for you to think about,
everybody does not want

00:12:04.544 --> 00:12:07.867
to just hear your problems all the time.

00:12:07.867 --> 00:12:10.700
(audience laughs)

00:12:13.675 --> 00:12:16.178
Now it's great to have a good friend

00:12:16.178 --> 00:12:18.953
that you can share with
but you don't have to

00:12:18.953 --> 00:12:23.597
share and share and share
and share and share.

00:12:23.597 --> 00:12:26.089
And share and share, and then
when you wear that one out,

00:12:26.089 --> 00:12:29.836
go find another one and
share and share and share.

00:12:29.836 --> 00:12:32.669
(audience laughs)

00:12:33.837 --> 00:12:36.070
So if you have a habit of just
talking about your problems

00:12:36.070 --> 00:12:39.737
all the time, it's time
to make a new habit,

00:12:41.252 --> 00:12:43.796
and that is to find
something good to talk about

00:12:43.796 --> 00:12:46.362
and I'll just throw this
out for good measure, too.

00:12:46.362 --> 00:12:48.057
Your friends don't want to just hear you

00:12:48.057 --> 00:12:50.333
talk about yourself all the time.

00:12:50.333 --> 00:12:52.630
And I remember God telling me
in the very, very beginning

00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:57.159
of our ministry, if you
can not complain about

00:12:57.159 --> 00:13:01.167
where you go to meetings,
the day will come

00:13:01.167 --> 00:13:03.938
when you'll be able to
go anywhere you want to

00:13:03.938 --> 00:13:08.319
and hold a meeting, well,
that's pretty much true today

00:13:08.319 --> 00:13:11.008
but I had to go through
a lot of rough places

00:13:11.008 --> 00:13:13.954
and difficult places, and
I think a lot of people,

00:13:13.954 --> 00:13:15.463
and I want you to listen
to me, a lot of people

00:13:15.463 --> 00:13:18.574
never get to where they want
to be because they'll never

00:13:18.574 --> 00:13:21.781
stop complaining about where they're at,

00:13:21.781 --> 00:13:25.324
I'ma say it again, a lot
of people will never get

00:13:25.324 --> 00:13:27.881
to where they want to be
because they will never stop

00:13:27.881 --> 00:13:32.048
complaining about where
they're at, the word complain

00:13:33.464 --> 00:13:36.961
means to remain or to stay overnight,

00:13:36.961 --> 00:13:39.007
so if you want to stay
right where you're at,

00:13:39.007 --> 00:13:41.254
just keep complaining about
it, and I can pretty much

00:13:41.254 --> 00:13:44.374
guarantee you that you'll still be there

00:13:44.374 --> 00:13:45.652
this time next year.

00:13:45.652 --> 00:13:49.870
I mean, can we believe
tonight that Jesus didn't die

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:53.870
so we could be wimpy and
whiny and barely going,

00:13:55.619 --> 00:13:57.968
I'm just so tired of
this, I just don't know

00:13:57.968 --> 00:14:02.135
if I can make it or not, Jesus (whines)

00:14:03.619 --> 00:14:06.455
(audience laughs)

00:14:06.455 --> 00:14:07.288
Come on.

00:14:12.276 --> 00:14:14.499
Bunch of people old before
their times because they look,

00:14:14.499 --> 00:14:17.400
you know, they're 40
and look like they're 90

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:19.381
because they worried themselves to death.

00:14:19.381 --> 00:14:22.131
(audience claps)

00:14:27.617 --> 00:14:29.420
I mean, come on, you stay
full of the Holy Ghost

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:31.838
and you're going to look
younger when you're 80

00:14:31.838 --> 00:14:33.374
than you did when you were 40.

00:14:33.374 --> 00:14:36.207
(audience cheers)

00:14:43.153 --> 00:14:46.736
Let's look at Acts
chapter one verse eight.

00:14:48.442 --> 00:14:52.609
(laughs) Look at this, "But
you shall receive power."

00:14:55.596 --> 00:14:58.019
I knew that God had power,
but I went to church

00:14:58.019 --> 00:15:02.731
for years and nobody told
me I could have any power.

00:15:02.731 --> 00:15:06.470
So just in case nobody's ever told you,

00:15:06.470 --> 00:15:09.674
I want to tell you in
this room and all of you

00:15:09.674 --> 00:15:12.189
watching by television
all around the world

00:15:12.189 --> 00:15:17.041
in these 63 languages this
program is translated into,

00:15:17.041 --> 00:15:20.771
whether you're in China or
Russia or India or Africa,

00:15:20.771 --> 00:15:23.043
you can have power.

00:15:23.043 --> 00:15:25.876
(audience cheers)

00:15:28.971 --> 00:15:33.217
God wants you to have power
to live your everyday life,

00:15:33.217 --> 00:15:36.083
where even when we are
loaded down with troubles,

00:15:36.083 --> 00:15:38.733
we can throw our shoulders
back and lift our head up

00:15:38.733 --> 00:15:41.313
and say I can do whatever
I need to do through Christ

00:15:41.313 --> 00:15:42.896
who strengthens me.

00:15:45.944 --> 00:15:49.073
I am not without an answer,
I am not without a way,

00:15:49.073 --> 00:15:52.382
because God is living in
me in close fellowship

00:15:52.382 --> 00:15:54.965
and he will show me what to do.

00:15:57.757 --> 00:15:59.448
If we don't understand the power of God,

00:15:59.448 --> 00:16:03.463
no wonder, being a Christian is so boring,

00:16:03.463 --> 00:16:05.587
there's nothing you can do.

00:16:05.587 --> 00:16:09.234
Let me just tell you
that I was so selfish,

00:16:09.234 --> 00:16:13.401
oh my gosh, I was so selfish,
I was always on my mind.

00:16:14.646 --> 00:16:17.479
(audience laughs)

00:16:18.408 --> 00:16:20.140
You know, if Dave was
going to go play golf,

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:24.338
the first thing I'd think
is, well, what about me?

00:16:24.338 --> 00:16:25.883
And if Dave was going to
watch a football game,

00:16:25.883 --> 00:16:27.550
well, what about me?

00:16:28.607 --> 00:16:31.042
The kids'd go outside with
Dave to play and I had work

00:16:31.042 --> 00:16:34.634
to do inside, you know, mind
you, I could've not worked

00:16:34.634 --> 00:16:36.139
and went out and enjoyed myself, but no,

00:16:36.139 --> 00:16:39.672
I wanted to work so I could
feel sorry for myself.

00:16:39.672 --> 00:16:42.505
(audience laughs)

00:16:44.361 --> 00:16:48.528
And everything was, well,
what about me, what about me,

00:16:49.385 --> 00:16:52.442
when's somebody going
to do something for me

00:16:52.442 --> 00:16:54.478
and I started early in the
morning, before I was even

00:16:54.478 --> 00:16:56.457
fully awake thinking about myself.

00:16:56.457 --> 00:16:59.559
(audience laughs)

00:16:59.559 --> 00:17:02.060
Any of you like that?

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:04.912
And so many many many years
ago I was laying in bed

00:17:04.912 --> 00:17:06.543
one morning, and I wasn't
even fully awake yet

00:17:06.543 --> 00:17:09.943
and I was thinking about
how I could get Dave to

00:17:09.943 --> 00:17:11.563
not do what he wanted to do that day

00:17:11.563 --> 00:17:14.913
and do what I wanted and,
you know, how I could maybe

00:17:14.913 --> 00:17:17.955
get the kids to do the
housework so I could just

00:17:17.955 --> 00:17:21.138
kind of chill and, you know, have fun,

00:17:21.138 --> 00:17:25.211
and it was like I was just
thinking about myself,

00:17:25.211 --> 00:17:28.617
just laying there in bed,
thinking about myself,

00:17:28.617 --> 00:17:30.415
and you know, that's a
dangerous way to start your day

00:17:30.415 --> 00:17:31.914
because however you get
started, that's usually

00:17:31.914 --> 00:17:35.008
the way things go the rest of the day,

00:17:35.008 --> 00:17:36.158
and you're much better off to lay in bed

00:17:36.158 --> 00:17:38.321
and purposely think, God, what can I do

00:17:38.321 --> 00:17:41.813
for somebody else today, how
can I be a greater blessing

00:17:41.813 --> 00:17:46.669
to my family, God, how can
I be a better wife today?

00:17:46.669 --> 00:17:47.885
The last time I asked God that,

00:17:47.885 --> 00:17:49.173
he told me to cook Dave some breakfast,

00:17:49.173 --> 00:17:52.319
I haven't asked that in a while.

00:17:52.319 --> 00:17:55.385
(audience laughs)

00:17:55.385 --> 00:17:58.415
'Cause I'm not into too much cooking

00:17:58.415 --> 00:18:00.167
and poor guy about fainted when I said

00:18:00.167 --> 00:18:03.329
I'm going to cook your breakfast, so.

00:18:03.329 --> 00:18:07.373
You got to be ready when you
ask God that kind of stuff

00:18:07.373 --> 00:18:10.205
but it's been life changing for me

00:18:10.205 --> 00:18:11.853
the principles that I'm
sharing with you tonight

00:18:11.853 --> 00:18:15.289
really has been one of the
key elements in my life

00:18:15.289 --> 00:18:17.512
that have gotten me from
where I was to where I am,

00:18:17.512 --> 00:18:18.821
so I'm laying there thinking about myself

00:18:18.821 --> 00:18:21.034
and I kind of had,
like, this little vision

00:18:21.034 --> 00:18:23.083
and the Holy Ghost began
to deal with me in my heart

00:18:23.083 --> 00:18:26.358
and he said, you know, the
enemy comes and starts putting

00:18:26.358 --> 00:18:31.044
thoughts in your head
real early in the morning

00:18:31.044 --> 00:18:35.211
and it's like he's getting
you wound up for the day,

00:18:36.212 --> 00:18:39.491
he said, you remind me
of this little robot,

00:18:39.491 --> 00:18:44.152
the devil comes and he's,
like, what about me,

00:18:44.152 --> 00:18:48.069
what about me, what about
me and what about me?

00:18:50.746 --> 00:18:52.367
And then you put your feet on the floor

00:18:52.367 --> 00:18:54.392
and this is the way you look
to me the rest of the day.

00:18:54.392 --> 00:18:56.057
(robotic voice) What
about me, what about me,

00:18:56.057 --> 00:18:59.144
what about me, what about me, beep beep,

00:18:59.144 --> 00:19:02.811
what about me, what
about me, what about me.

00:19:05.549 --> 00:19:06.554
Thank you guys so much for watching,

00:19:06.554 --> 00:19:10.452
I made this video because
Natasha O'Meara asked me to

00:19:10.452 --> 00:19:11.451
so if there's a famous entrepreneur

00:19:11.451 --> 00:19:12.451
that you want me to profile next,

00:19:12.451 --> 00:19:14.730
leave it in the comments below
and I'll see what I can do.

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:16.387
I'll also love to know what did Joyce say

00:19:16.387 --> 00:19:18.157
that had the biggest impact on you,

00:19:18.157 --> 00:19:20.167
which rule did you love the most and why,

00:19:20.167 --> 00:19:21.929
leave it in the comments,
I'm going to join

00:19:21.929 --> 00:19:24.386
in the discussion, finally,
want to give a quick shoutout

00:19:24.386 --> 00:19:26.761
to MeGaPuRe, thank you so
much for picking up a copy

00:19:26.761 --> 00:19:29.551
of my book, Your One Word,
and making that awesome

00:19:29.551 --> 00:19:32.047
Youtube video on your channel,
I really really really

00:19:32.047 --> 00:19:35.169
appreciate the support and
hope you're enjoying the book.

00:19:35.169 --> 00:19:37.752
(gentle music)

00:19:40.230 --> 00:19:41.699
So thank you guys again for watching,

00:19:41.699 --> 00:19:43.781
I believe in you, I hope
you continue to believe

00:19:43.781 --> 00:19:47.611
in yourself and whatever
your one word is, much love,

00:19:47.611 --> 00:19:49.111
I'll see you soon.

00:19:55.522 --> 00:19:59.557
- You know, we all have really
the same amount of time,

00:19:59.557 --> 00:20:03.242
each of us gets 24 hours every day,

00:20:03.242 --> 00:20:06.112
we don't get any more,
we don't get any less.

00:20:06.112 --> 00:20:08.703
Well, why is it that some
people can do so much

00:20:08.703 --> 00:20:11.799
with their time and
other people don't seem

00:20:11.799 --> 00:20:15.602
to ever accomplish what
they set out to accomplish

00:20:15.602 --> 00:20:19.349
with their time, we hear
this comment all the time,

00:20:19.349 --> 00:20:21.436
or we hear ourselves
saying it, I know I say it,

00:20:21.436 --> 00:20:24.919
where did all the time go, I can't believe

00:20:24.919 --> 00:20:29.086
this day has gone, I can't
believe it's already spring,

00:20:30.129 --> 00:20:32.488
I can't believe it's
Christmas, and we hear that

00:20:32.488 --> 00:20:36.405
all the time, well, where
does all the time go?

00:20:37.291 --> 00:20:41.020
To be honest, I think we
should know where our time goes

00:20:41.020 --> 00:20:43.512
and one of the things
that I've formed the habit

00:20:43.512 --> 00:20:45.572
of doing, I don't do it every
single day, but this really

00:20:45.572 --> 00:20:49.739
helps me, is people who live
busy lives, fast-paced lives,

00:20:50.883 --> 00:20:53.283
sometimes a whole day can go by in a blur

00:20:53.283 --> 00:20:54.961
and you know you were busy
but you're not really sure

00:20:54.961 --> 00:20:57.184
what you did, you did it all so fast

00:20:57.184 --> 00:20:59.958
that you can't even hardly
remember what you did,

00:20:59.958 --> 00:21:01.676
and one of the things that I enjoy doing

00:21:01.676 --> 00:21:03.570
is just laying in bed for
a few minutes at night

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:06.752
before I drift off to
sleep and actually starting

00:21:06.752 --> 00:21:10.587
with my morning in my
thoughts and thinking about

00:21:10.587 --> 00:21:14.004
everything that I did that day, I got up,

00:21:16.725 --> 00:21:19.808
made my coffee, went up to my office,

00:21:21.915 --> 00:21:24.882
had some time with God,
looked over my calendar,

00:21:24.882 --> 00:21:27.353
you know, whatever it was
that I did, I like to go

00:21:27.353 --> 00:21:29.755
through those things because
then it actually helps me

00:21:29.755 --> 00:21:33.580
remember what I'm doing with my life.

00:21:33.580 --> 00:21:35.516
I don't want my life to go by in a blur

00:21:35.516 --> 00:21:38.201
and I don't think you do either, I believe

00:21:38.201 --> 00:21:42.119
that every day that God gives us is a gift

00:21:42.119 --> 00:21:46.377
and I think we should open
that gift fully and completely,

00:21:46.377 --> 00:21:49.044
enjoy every single moment of it.

00:21:50.092 --> 00:21:51.877
Some people don't enjoy
their lives because they feel

00:21:51.877 --> 00:21:54.362
like they have too much
to do all the time,

00:21:54.362 --> 00:21:56.581
well, then make some changes, don't let

00:21:56.581 --> 00:22:00.405
what everybody else wants run your life,

00:22:00.405 --> 00:22:03.581
take your life back, I
think under God's direction

00:22:03.581 --> 00:22:05.802
and leadership, we need to
take charge of our lives

00:22:05.802 --> 00:22:07.637
and we need to start putting our time

00:22:07.637 --> 00:22:11.057
into what we want to put it
into instead of just what

00:22:11.057 --> 00:22:14.581
everybody else wants us to put it into

00:22:14.581 --> 00:22:16.138
and I don't mean by that
that we don't do things

00:22:16.138 --> 00:22:18.234
for people, we all should
be busy doing things

00:22:18.234 --> 00:22:21.069
for other people, we all
should serve, we have jobs,

00:22:21.069 --> 00:22:24.218
we have responsibilities,
but don't just let all

00:22:24.218 --> 00:22:28.451
your circumstances rule you
and everybody else's decisions

00:22:28.451 --> 00:22:32.695
about what they want you
to do for them rule you,

00:22:32.695 --> 00:22:34.274
take your life back,

00:22:34.274 --> 00:22:36.142
so I want to share with
you a little exercise

00:22:36.142 --> 00:22:39.332
that I think you can do at any time,

00:22:39.332 --> 00:22:41.290
I've been doing this and I'm
finding it very refreshing

00:22:41.290 --> 00:22:45.895
and that is simply to
stop several times a day

00:22:45.895 --> 00:22:49.978
and just say, Lord, I want
to just live this moment

00:22:51.875 --> 00:22:55.217
that I'm in, you know, so often we don't,

00:22:55.217 --> 00:22:57.790
we're breathing, but
we're not really living

00:22:57.790 --> 00:23:02.765
the moment that we're in, we're
in such a frustrated uproar

00:23:02.765 --> 00:23:05.129
over all the things that
are going on in our lives

00:23:05.129 --> 00:23:08.700
that so much of our day just flies by

00:23:08.700 --> 00:23:10.802
and at night we don't even
really know what we did

00:23:10.802 --> 00:23:12.397
but we know it was pretty frustrating

00:23:12.397 --> 00:23:15.327
and we didn't enjoy all
that much of the day

00:23:15.327 --> 00:23:18.366
and I think it's a very good exercise

00:23:18.366 --> 00:23:20.509
to stop several times a day and just say,

00:23:20.509 --> 00:23:22.110
now Lord, I'm going to
enter into this moment

00:23:22.110 --> 00:23:26.277
and really just live this
moment and to think about

00:23:27.869 --> 00:23:30.545
and to tell God what
you're thankful for at that

00:23:30.545 --> 00:23:33.128
particular moment in your life.

00:23:34.279 --> 00:23:37.740
And there was a certain man, verse five,

00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:39.818
who had suffered with a
deep seated and a lingering

00:23:39.818 --> 00:23:42.850
disorder for 38 years, a
deep seated and a lingering

00:23:42.850 --> 00:23:47.017
disorder for 38 years, and
it's this man right here.

00:23:50.704 --> 00:23:54.704
And Jesus said a most
amazing thing to this man,

00:23:56.130 --> 00:23:59.859
when Jesus noticed him
lying there helpless,

00:23:59.859 --> 00:24:01.710
knowing that he'd already been a long time

00:24:01.710 --> 00:24:04.847
in that condition, he
said to him, do you want

00:24:04.847 --> 00:24:09.014
to become well, well, what
kind of a question is that?

00:24:13.419 --> 00:24:15.646
Do you want to get well?

00:24:15.646 --> 00:24:16.804
- Sure.

00:24:16.804 --> 00:24:19.637
(audience laughs)

00:24:21.382 --> 00:24:23.086
- And then Jesus goes a little deeper,

00:24:23.086 --> 00:24:27.253
he says, are you really in
earnest about getting well?

00:24:30.586 --> 00:24:34.153
And then the most amazing
thing, the invalid answered him

00:24:34.153 --> 00:24:35.153
and said ...

00:24:37.908 --> 00:24:41.658
- I don't have anybody
to put me in the pool.

00:24:42.678 --> 00:24:43.676
- [Joyce] And?

00:24:43.676 --> 00:24:46.200
- Every time I try,
somebody gets in front of me

00:24:46.200 --> 00:24:49.367
and they get their healing and not me.

00:24:50.892 --> 00:24:53.484
- So when Jesus said to him,
do you really want to get well,

00:24:53.484 --> 00:24:56.375
he said, I have nobody
to put me into the pool.

00:24:56.375 --> 00:24:59.587
(audience laughs)

00:24:59.587 --> 00:25:01.935
He was waiting for
somebody to do it for him.

00:25:01.935 --> 00:25:04.119
You say, well, Joyce,
give the guy a break,

00:25:04.119 --> 00:25:08.286
he was crippled, well, I
want to tell you something,

00:25:09.627 --> 00:25:12.745
in 38 years, I could have
done a lot of wiggling.

00:25:12.745 --> 00:25:15.495
(audience claps)

00:25:20.984 --> 00:25:23.121
(laughs) I mean, in 38
years, if you only wiggled

00:25:23.121 --> 00:25:26.121
a little part of an inch every year,

00:25:27.428 --> 00:25:29.898
I mean, he had 365 days to wiggle.

00:25:29.898 --> 00:25:32.731
(audience laughs)

00:25:34.861 --> 00:25:38.300
Just a little bit, but the
only thing he could say

00:25:38.300 --> 00:25:42.467
to Jesus, was, there's
nobody to put me in the pool,

00:25:44.132 --> 00:25:47.016
and when I try to get up,
somebody gets ahead of me.

00:25:47.016 --> 00:25:50.266
Now Jesus didn't say, oh, you poor man,

00:25:51.449 --> 00:25:55.992
I cannot believe that you
have been laying here 38 years

00:25:55.992 --> 00:25:58.127
and nobody has put you into the pool,

00:25:58.127 --> 00:26:00.178
that is really terrible.

00:26:00.178 --> 00:26:01.178
- I know.

00:26:01.178 --> 00:26:03.729
- It's really bad, isn't it?

00:26:03.729 --> 00:26:05.196
- Yeah.

00:26:05.196 --> 00:26:07.363
- [Joyce] Just really bad?

00:26:08.627 --> 00:26:10.430
- I'm glad you're starting
to see things my way.

00:26:10.430 --> 00:26:13.263
(audience laughs)

00:26:14.394 --> 00:26:16.977
(Joyce laughs)

00:26:22.190 --> 00:26:24.458
He's getting this, he's
actually got, I think,

00:26:24.458 --> 00:26:28.625
tears in his eyes, now, you
know, Jesus being loving

00:26:31.526 --> 00:26:33.644
and kind, I would think that
he would have just said,

00:26:33.644 --> 00:26:35.719
that is the most horrible
thing I ever heard,

00:26:35.719 --> 00:26:37.786
I am going to fix your problem tonight,

00:26:37.786 --> 00:26:41.786
but here is what Jesus
said to him, verse eight,

00:26:43.354 --> 00:26:46.187
Jesus said to him, get up, get up!

00:26:48.491 --> 00:26:50.604
(audience cheers)

00:26:50.604 --> 00:26:51.437
Get up!

00:26:52.437 --> 00:26:55.236
And pick up your bed and walk, go home

00:26:55.236 --> 00:26:57.975
with that mess you've
made in the last 38 years,

00:26:57.975 --> 00:27:01.558
get out of here and
live your life, get up!

